yaml/string/plain
description: Bare unquoted text
- >
  The plain concrete is bare text, no quotes - an unquoted token whose content resolves to no
  other type is a string. Punctuation YAML claims for itself (`: ` and ` #` inside, an
  indicator character at the start) forces one of the quoted concretes:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  e: just text, one line
